# Configuration-Driven School ERP

- Configuration > Customization > Development
- Never write school-specific Java or Angular code
- Every feature must support Feature Flags
- Every screen must support dynamic field configuration
- Every report must be template-driven
- Every workflow must be configurable
- Every business rule must use the Rule Engine
- Every subscription must control features through configuration
- Org / branch / academic session independent settings
- White-label without code changes
- Metadata-driven UI where feasible
- Multi-tenancy and horizontal scalability from day one
- School management is a separate Angular UI (`apps/school-ui`) and dedicated microservices (`services/*`)
- Audit every configuration change with rollback support

See `docs/IMPLEMENTATION_RULES.md`.
